{"parentUuid":"e601df12-99e1-430e-b4af-dc7e84c8420c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>11670769 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2d97180b-d370-41c6-ac30-c13f753682ad","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:19.249Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>11670769 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"2d97180b-d370-41c6-ac30-c13f753682ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvuoTgmiybi8iEmQ4xi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JkyCd3nrFVs39onC3y1yoF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:<socket>","summary":"Round 3 fixed, Plan e2e, ElevenLabs live","message":"Round 3 is fixed, the Plan e2e is in, and ElevenLabs is live as 8260be8. Smoke and the live demo e2e both pass.\n\nFresh-eyes round 3 scored 5/10. I've capped rounds at 3, as you asked.\n- **Main cause:** site.css was global, and SvelteKit keeps it loaded after a client-side move from the website into /app/.\n  - The site's .hero rule (a navy fill) covered your photo on Send.\n  - The site's .art rule (230 px tall) squashed the onboarding photo.\n  - Fix: every site.css rule is now scoped under .site. I checked by navigating site → demo and site → app.\n- **Also fixed:**\n  - Sheets: a close button on every sheet, and the menu stops 72 px short of the top so there's backdrop to tap.\n  - Demo:\n    - Conditions now go through the real parser, so nonsense gets \"I didn't catch that\", and the banner shows the read-back.\n    - After the friend's view: \"Back to you, {name}. One more yes: 2 in.\"\n    - Benny's yes now shows before \"It's lit\".\n  - Plan dates now stack on phones.\n  - Honesty: the privacy page said the weather lookup happens only for Plans. It also happens when Home opens, and the line now says so.\n- **Still open:** 8 issues, ranked, in docs/research/fresh-eyes-2026-10-11.md. Round 4 runs after the feature work.\n\n**Plan e2e (new, npm run e2e:plan), 12/12 passing.** It runs Home → P1, which now loads on demand → P2 → send. Amor answers \"step 3 or smaller\" through the read-back, and Kai says yes. At the deadline the plan solves at step 3 and lights for both phones. Then Amor fades once.\n- **Real bug it found:** on a phone with no saved first name, Send on P2 silently did nothing. P2 now asks for the name, as H3 does.\n\n**ElevenLabs (ADR-0027)**\n- **Warm compass voice:** 54 fixed lines (distances, directions, close, hold flat, no GPS), recorded once by scripts/gen-voice.ts with the premade voice Sarah.\n  - Cost: 698 of the free 10,000 characters, and 684 KB in total.\n  - Privacy: no names or places, so nothing of anyone's reaches ElevenLabs.\n  - Opt-in under My needs, with a \"Hear it\" sample. When it's on, the clips are cached on the phone so it works offline. The phone's own voice is the fallback.\n- **Voice Spark:** \"Say it\" on the Spark screen.\n  - You tap, and it records up to 10 s of your own voice. Scribe v2 turns that into words for you to edit.\n  - The audio is zero-filled and never stored. The server has a daily cap.\n  - Live probe: 0.72 s, word for word.\n  - The privacy page and NOTICE are updated. I don't claim zero retention, because ElevenLabs offers that on enterprise plans only.\n  - Never other people, never conversations.\n- **Not built:** reading the invite aloud in the warm voice. It would mean sending sealed text out of the phone, so I left it out on purpose.\n\n**Tests:** all pass.\n- Unit: 674/62/26. The new tests cover the clip mapping and that every clip shipped; the server voice tests cover off without a key, 415, 413, null on failure, and the cap.\n- e2e: sparks now includes Say it, using a synthetic mic because headless Chrome hangs on audio-only getUserMedia. demo, plan, loop, telegram, field 27/27, pwa and kit a11y 0 all pass.\n- Lighthouse is 100 on all five pages. JS budget: /g/ 149 KB and /app 149.5 KB, because the Plan screens and Say it now load on demand.\n\n**Next:** the website feature cards and the \"Built with\" strip.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:<socket>","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Round 3 is fixed, the Plan e2e is in, and ElevenL…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3175,"cache_read_input_tokens":427639,"output_tokens":1450,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3175,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1450,"cache_read_input_tokens":427639,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3175},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JkyCd3nrFVs39onC3y1yoF":{"to":"uds:<socket>","summary":"Round 3 fixed, Plan e2e, ElevenLabs live","message":"Round 3 is fixed, the Plan e2e is in, and ElevenLabs is live as 8260be8. Smoke and the live demo e2e both pass.\n\nFresh-eyes round 3 scored 5/10. I've capped rounds at 3, as you asked.\n- **Main cause:** site.css was global, and SvelteKit keeps it loaded after a client-side move from the website into /app/.\n  - The site's .hero rule (a navy fill) covered your photo on Send.\n  - The site's .art rule (230 px tall) squashed the onboarding photo.\n  - Fix: every site.css rule is now scoped under .site. I checked by navigating site → demo and site → app.\n- **Also fixed:**\n  - Sheets: a close button on every sheet, and the menu stops 72 px short of the top so there's backdrop to tap.\n  - Demo:\n    - Conditions now go through the real parser, so nonsense gets \"I didn't catch that\", and the banner shows the read-back.\n    - After the friend's view: \"Back to you, {name}. One more yes: 2 in.\"\n    - Benny's yes now shows before \"It's lit\".\n  - Plan dates now stack on phones.\n  - Honesty: the privacy page said the weather lookup happens only for Plans. It also happens when Home opens, and the line now says so.\n- **Still open:** 8 issues, ranked, in docs/research/fresh-eyes-2026-10-11.md. Round 4 runs after the feature work.\n\n**Plan e2e (new, npm run e2e:plan), 12/12 passing.** It runs Home → P1, which now loads on demand → P2 → send. Amor answers \"step 3 or smaller\" through the read-back, and Kai says yes. At the deadline the plan solves at step 3 and lights for both phones. Then Amor fades once.\n- **Real bug it found:** on a phone with no saved first name, Send on P2 silently did nothing. P2 now asks for the name, as H3 does.\n\n**ElevenLabs (ADR-0027)**\n- **Warm compass voice:** 54 fixed lines (distances, directions, close, hold flat, no GPS), recorded once by scripts/gen-voice.ts with the premade voice Sarah.\n  - Cost: 698 of the free 10,000 characters, and 684 KB in total.\n  - Privacy: no names or places, so nothing of anyone's reaches ElevenLabs.\n  - Opt-in under My needs, with a \"Hear it\" sample. When it's on, the clips are cached on the phone so it works offline. The phone's own voice is the fallback.\n- **Voice Spark:** \"Say it\" on the Spark screen.\n  - You tap, and it records up to 10 s of your own voice. Scribe v2 turns that into words for you to edit.\n  - The audio is zero-filled and never stored. The server has a daily cap.\n  - Live probe: 0.72 s, word for word.\n  - The privacy page and NOTICE are updated. I don't claim zero retention, because ElevenLabs offers that on enterprise plans only.\n  - Never other people, never conversations.\n- **Not built:** reading the invite aloud in the warm voice. It would mean sending sealed text out of the phone, so I left it out on purpose.\n\n**Tests:** all pass.\n- Unit: 674/62/26. The new tests cover the clip mapping and that every clip shipped; the server voice tests cover off without a key, 415, 413, null on failure, and the cap.\n- e2e: sparks now includes Say it, using a synthetic mic because headless Chrome hangs on audio-only getUserMedia. demo, plan, loop, telegram, field 27/27, pwa and kit a11y 0 all pass.\n- Lighthouse is 100 on all five pages. JS budget: /g/ 149 KB and /app 149.5 KB, because the Plan screens and Say it now load on demand.\n\n**Next:** the website feature cards and the \"Built with\" strip."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2f287556-4ba7-4be1-967c-ba8e7d9c4a0a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvuoSeX4Hyvu6pQyQKcB","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a5cf0e5-fd26-40f3-bce2-31ec545ba6db","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:33.483Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"8a5cf0e5-fd26-40f3-bce2-31ec545ba6db","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f93043c4-458a-4d94-b158-9e5f79350398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkyCd3nrFVs39onC3y1yoF","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"“Round 3 fixed, Plan e2e, ElevenLabs live” → uds:<socket>; in that session's inbox, not yet read by its Claude — a [Cross-session delivery notice] follows if that session holds it (usually a different permission mode) or refuses it\",\"msg_id\":\"51850d51-ad70-450c-9860-b1990bc5f7a0\"}"}]}]},"uuid":"84013ef3-4c7c-4203-8c7c-f16237465961","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:34.305Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"“Round 3 fixed, Plan e2e, ElevenLabs live” → uds:<socket>; in that session's inbox, not yet read by its Claude — a [Cross-session delivery notice] follows if that session holds it (usually a different permission mode) or refuses it","display":"“Round 3 fixed, Plan e2e, ElevenLabs live” → uds:<socket>","msg_id":"51850d51-ad70-450c-9860-b1990bc5f7a0"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2f287556-4ba7-4be1-967c-ba8e7d9c4a0a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":7,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":27},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a5cf0e5-fd26-40f3-bce2-31ec545ba6db","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"84013ef3-4c7c-4203-8c7c-f16237465961","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>11667891 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0d6e99ec-3c27-46bf-8069-5bcf694ae2f8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:34.311Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>11667891 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"0d6e99ec-3c27-46bf-8069-5bcf694ae2f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvupa8FdhX3RYEm28TZU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fresh-eyes round 3 fixes, the Plan e2e and ElevenLabs are all live as 8260be8. The smoke check and the demo test against the live site both pass.\n\n**Round 3 (5/10, the last round per the manager's pacing):**\n- **Main bug:** the website's styles were global, and they stay loaded when you tap from the website into the app. Two of the site's rules hit the app's own screens: one put a navy block over your photo on Send, the other squashed the onboarding photo. Every website style is now limited to website pages.\n- **Also fixed:**\n  - Sheets have a close button, and the menu leaves room to tap outside it.\n  - In the demo, conditions go through the real parser, and it says \"Back to you\" after the friend's view.\n  - The Plan date fields stack on phones.\n  - The privacy page said the weather lookup happens only for Plans. It also happens when Home opens, and it now says so.\n- **Still open:** 8 smaller issues, ranked, in `docs/research/fresh-eyes-2026-10-11.md`. Round 4 runs after the feature work.\n\n**Plan e2e (`npm run e2e:plan`, 12/12):** it covers creating a plan, a condition, the deadline solve and a fade. It found a real bug: on a phone with no saved first name, sending a Plan silently did nothing. The Plan screen now asks for the name, the same way the Send screen does.\n\n**ElevenLabs:**\n- **Warm compass voice:** 54 fixed lines (distances, directions, \"You're close\"), recorded once and shipped with the app.\n  - Cost: 698 of the free 10,000 characters a month, once.\n  - Privacy: no names or places, so nothing of yours reaches ElevenLabs.\n  - It's opt-in under My needs, with a \"Hear it\" sample, and works offline once turned on. The phone's own voice is the fallback.\n- **Voice Spark:** a \"Say it\" button on the Spark screen.\n  - You tap, and it records up to 10 seconds of your own voice. Scribe turns that into words for you to edit.\n  - Flare keeps no audio. On the live site it came back word for word in 0.72 s.\n  - It never records other people or conversations.\n- **Not built:** reading the invite aloud in the warm voice. That would send encrypted invite text off the phone, so I left it out on purpose.\n- **Docs:** the privacy page, the NOTICE credit and ADR-0027 are updated. The privacy page doesn't claim ElevenLabs deletes recordings, because that guarantee is only on its enterprise plans.\n\n**Checks:** all unit tests and e2e suites pass, Lighthouse is 100 on all five site pages, and both app pages are under the 150 KB JS budget (149 KB and 149.5 KB).\n\nNext up are the website feature cards and the \"Built with\" strip. Still yours to decide: Google billing, DigitalOcean billing, and making the repo public."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1626,"cache_read_input_tokens":430814,"output_tokens":980,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1626,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":430814,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1626},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5adc16fa-a1fd-4161-adaa-35e3c8179b15","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvupYy4GYAx63yzM2K4T","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae497af9-e2f7-4a0c-85b1-dbc20e33a187","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:44.449Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:19:46.760Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" hop-chain=\"e1bd9b33a07bd8c38e68ae6a,d6d9bf2e945799a80139a5bf,e1bd9b33a07bd8c38e68ae6a,d6d9bf2e945799a80139a5bf\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nApproved. The pre-recorded compass voice is a smart privacy design, and so is leaving out the invite read-aloud. The scoped site.css fix explains a lot of round 3.\n\nAfter the feature cards, in this order:\n1. Voice Flares and the Crew Atlas\n2. Automations (Plan auto-solve and reminders, weather-aware Ember, opt-in golden-hour nudge, weekly recap, \"Tell the chat\")\n3. Sentry depth (Mastra agent runs plus server error and performance)\n4. Page audit\n5. Fresh-eyes round 4\n6. Post media recapture\n7. Finish the post draft\n\nThe JS budget is at 149.5 of 150, so get back about 10 KB of headroom when you can.\n</cross-session-message>"}
