{"parentUuid":"76ca147b-f56b-434b-a46e-9a7369bed7a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvx6QH6pyRCF145YMLUk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Voice Flare works end to end. Committing it, then on to the Crew Atlas:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":527531,"output_tokens":3121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":449},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3121,"cache_read_input_tokens":527531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b48b167-826c-4e15-91dd-6583b2246e13","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfvx6P3gHNEE5iCR9BZuq","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7296046-eb05-44b0-b2b9-bc73a95cbe4e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:49:29.993Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"c7296046-eb05-44b0-b2b9-bc73a95cbe4e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvx6QH6pyRCF145YMLUk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EWgt8cJHFn6ZLJsUg8hWmz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && cat > docs/architecture/adr/0028-voice-flares.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-0028: Voice Flares, the invite from what the host says, on our laptop\n\nStatus: Accepted (Sun 2026-10-11).\n\n## Context\nA Flare starts with a photo, and Gemma 4 on the hub writes the invite and the place line from it. Some people can't take a useful photo: people who are blind or have low vision, or who are in the dark or have their hands full. The backlog asked for Voice Flares (#9): say it, and Gemma 4 writes the invite.\n\n## What we checked\n- **Ollama reports audio.** For `gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M`, Ollama 0.40.2 lists the capabilities `completion, vision, audio, tools, thinking` (`/api/show`).\n- **Audio goes in `images`.** The model hears audio passed base64 in a message's `images` field. A field named `audio` is ignored.\n- **Transcription works.** One of our own warm-voice clips came back as \"You're close. Look around.\" in 2 s.\n- **The voice prompt works.** Voice prompt v1, given a `say` recording of \"I'm at the pond in Ford Woods Park. Come sit on the bench with me, the light is really nice.\", answered `{\"invite\": \"Meet at the pond bench.\", \"alt\": \"The pond in Fordwoods Park has nice light to sit on the bench.\"}` in 3.7 s. A second sentence (\"Walk to the cider mill after work? I'm by the big oak at Fairlane Green.\") took 3.5 s.\n\n## Decision\n- **Phone.** The camera screen has \"Say it instead\".\n  - One tap starts recording and a second tap stops it. It stops by itself at 10 s.\n  - The phone converts the clip to 16 kHz mono 16-bit WAV (`lib/voice/flare.ts`) and sends it once to `POST /api/v1/drafts/voice`.\n  - Nothing is kept on the phone, and the microphone is released at once.\n  - The control loads only when the camera screen shows (JS budget).\n- **Server.** WAV only (RIFF....WAVE), at most 400 KB.\n  - It relays the audio to the hub as a `voice-draft` job (asyncapi `voiceJob`: a header, then one binary frame) with an 8 s budget, like the ladder.\n  - It runs `enforce()` again on the answer.\n  - The buffer is zero-filled on every path, and nothing is stored or logged.\n  - The words heard never come back, only `{invite, alt, tier}`.\n  - It counts `tier_ran.voice.{tier}`.\n- **No cloud tier.** A voice is more personal than a photo, so it stays on the open model on our own laptop. If the hub is absent, slow or hears no place, the response is `tier: rules`. The phone then says \"Didn't catch a place. Take a photo or try again.\"\n- **Hub.** The frame must start with RIFF, or the result is `bad_audio` and the model is never called. The hub uses voice prompt v1 (`packages/shared/src/prompts/voice.ts`): only places and things the person said, no names, faces or bodies, and an empty answer when no place is heard. It runs `enforce()` and makes no retry: at temperature 0 a retry gives the same answer. The audio is zero-filled after the job.\n- **Send.** With no photo, Send shows the invite over the outdoor scenery and asks for the place if the map didn't name one.\n\n## Tests\n- `apps/hub/test/voice.test.ts`:\n  - audio in, a guarded draft out, with the voice prompt and the audio passed as media;\n  - an empty answer is `unusable_answer`;\n  - a frame that isn't WAV is `bad_audio` and never reaches the model.\n- `apps/server/test/contract.test.ts` (`draftFromVoice`): the template when no hub is connected, 400 for a file that isn't WAV, 413, and 415.\n- `apps/web/test/e2e/voice-flare.ts` runs on the real stack on this Mac: real server, real hub, real Gemma 4.\n  - The `say` fixture plays in as the microphone. A real MediaRecorder records it and the phone converts it to WAV (167 KB).\n  - \"Meet at the pond bench\" comes back in 3.3 s, and Send shows it over the scenery with no photo.\n\n## Consequences\n- A person who can't take a photo can still send a Flare by speaking for 10 seconds, and their voice goes only to our own laptop.\n- Asyncapi gains `voiceJob` and `voiceBytes`, and the result error enum gains `bad_audio`. A hub on the old code ignores the job, and the server falls back to the template after 8 s.\nEOF\nprintf '| [0028](0028-voice-flares.md) | Voice Flares: say where you are, Gemma 4 on the hub writes the invite from the audio (WAV in Ollama images); hub only, no audio kept | Accepted |\\n' >> docs/architecture/adr/README.md\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='''    \"site.privacy.l.voiceFlare\": {\n      \"text\": \"If you say your Flare instead of taking a photo, up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link, like a photo. Gemma 4 writes the invite from it. Nothing is kept, and the words it heard never come back.\",\n      \"kind\": \"prose\",\n      \"where\": \"site W4 (ADR-0028)\"\n    },\n    \"site.privacy.l.sleep\": {'''\ns=s.replace('    \"site.privacy.l.sleep\": {',add,1); json.loads(s); open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/content/02-copy-deck.md'\nL=open(p).read().split('\\n')\nfor i,l in enumerate(L):\n  if l.startswith('| `site.privacy.l.sleep` |'):\n    L.insert(i,\"| `site.privacy.l.voiceFlare` | If you say your Flare instead of taking a photo, up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link, like a photo. Gemma 4 writes the invite from it. Nothing is kept, and the words it heard never come back. | prose | 45 | | site W4 | ADR-0028 |\"); break\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(L))\np='apps/web/src/routes/(site)/privacy/+page.svelte'\ns=open(p).read(); s=s.replace('''    \"site.privacy.l.voice\",''','''    \"site.privacy.l.voice\",\n    \"site.privacy.l.voiceFlare\",''',1); open(p,'w').write(s)\np='package.json'\ns=open(p).read(); s=s.replace('''    \"e2e:plan\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/plan.ts\",''','''    \"e2e:plan\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/plan.ts\",\n    \"e2e:voice\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/voice-flare.ts\",''',1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; npx biome check --write . >/dev/null 2>&1; npm run lint 2>&1 | grep -c \"×\"; npm test 2>&1 | grep \"Tests \"","description":"ADR-0028, privacy line, script; lint and tests","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":527531,"output_tokens":3121,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":449},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3121,"cache_read_input_tokens":527531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EWgt8cJHFn6ZLJsUg8hWmz":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && cat > docs/architecture/adr/0028-voice-flares.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-0028: Voice Flares, the invite from what the host says, on our laptop\n\nStatus: Accepted (Sun 2026-10-11).\n\n## Context\nA Flare starts with a photo, and Gemma 4 on the hub writes the invite and the place line from it. Some people can't take a useful photo: people who are blind or have low vision, or who are in the dark or have their hands full. The backlog asked for Voice Flares (#9): say it, and Gemma 4 writes the invite.\n\n## What we checked\n- **Ollama reports audio.** For `gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M`, Ollama 0.40.2 lists the capabilities `completion, vision, audio, tools, thinking` (`/api/show`).\n- **Audio goes in `images`.** The model hears audio passed base64 in a message's `images` field. A field named `audio` is ignored.\n- **Transcription works.** One of our own warm-voice clips came back as \"You're close. Look around.\" in 2 s.\n- **The voice prompt works.** Voice prompt v1, given a `say` recording of \"I'm at the pond in Ford Woods Park. Come sit on the bench with me, the light is really nice.\", answered `{\"invite\": \"Meet at the pond bench.\", \"alt\": \"The pond in Fordwoods Park has nice light to sit on the bench.\"}` in 3.7 s. A second sentence (\"Walk to the cider mill after work? I'm by the big oak at Fairlane Green.\") took 3.5 s.\n\n## Decision\n- **Phone.** The camera screen has \"Say it instead\".\n  - One tap starts recording and a second tap stops it. It stops by itself at 10 s.\n  - The phone converts the clip to 16 kHz mono 16-bit WAV (`lib/voice/flare.ts`) and sends it once to `POST /api/v1/drafts/voice`.\n  - Nothing is kept on the phone, and the microphone is released at once.\n  - The control loads only when the camera screen shows (JS budget).\n- **Server.** WAV only (RIFF....WAVE), at most 400 KB.\n  - It relays the audio to the hub as a `voice-draft` job (asyncapi `voiceJob`: a header, then one binary frame) with an 8 s budget, like the ladder.\n  - It runs `enforce()` again on the answer.\n  - The buffer is zero-filled on every path, and nothing is stored or logged.\n  - The words heard never come back, only `{invite, alt, tier}`.\n  - It counts `tier_ran.voice.{tier}`.\n- **No cloud tier.** A voice is more personal than a photo, so it stays on the open model on our own laptop. If the hub is absent, slow or hears no place, the response is `tier: rules`. The phone then says \"Didn't catch a place. Take a photo or try again.\"\n- **Hub.** The frame must start with RIFF, or the result is `bad_audio` and the model is never called. The hub uses voice prompt v1 (`packages/shared/src/prompts/voice.ts`): only places and things the person said, no names, faces or bodies, and an empty answer when no place is heard. It runs `enforce()` and makes no retry: at temperature 0 a retry gives the same answer. The audio is zero-filled after the job.\n- **Send.** With no photo, Send shows the invite over the outdoor scenery and asks for the place if the map didn't name one.\n\n## Tests\n- `apps/hub/test/voice.test.ts`:\n  - audio in, a guarded draft out, with the voice prompt and the audio passed as media;\n  - an empty answer is `unusable_answer`;\n  - a frame that isn't WAV is `bad_audio` and never reaches the model.\n- `apps/server/test/contract.test.ts` (`draftFromVoice`): the template when no hub is connected, 400 for a file that isn't WAV, 413, and 415.\n- `apps/web/test/e2e/voice-flare.ts` runs on the real stack on this Mac: real server, real hub, real Gemma 4.\n  - The `say` fixture plays in as the microphone. A real MediaRecorder records it and the phone converts it to WAV (167 KB).\n  - \"Meet at the pond bench\" comes back in 3.3 s, and Send shows it over the scenery with no photo.\n\n## Consequences\n- A person who can't take a photo can still send a Flare by speaking for 10 seconds, and their voice goes only to our own laptop.\n- Asyncapi gains `voiceJob` and `voiceBytes`, and the result error enum gains `bad_audio`. A hub on the old code ignores the job, and the server falls back to the template after 8 s.\nEOF\nprintf '| [0028](0028-voice-flares.md) | Voice Flares: say where you are, Gemma 4 on the hub writes the invite from the audio (WAV in Ollama images); hub only, no audio kept | Accepted |\\n' >> docs/architecture/adr/README.md\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='''    \"site.privacy.l.voiceFlare\": {\n      \"text\": \"If you say your Flare instead of taking a photo, up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link, like a photo. Gemma 4 writes the invite from it. Nothing is kept, and the words it heard never come back.\",\n      \"kind\": \"prose\",\n      \"where\": \"site W4 (ADR-0028)\"\n    },\n    \"site.privacy.l.sleep\": {'''\ns=s.replace('    \"site.privacy.l.sleep\": {',add,1); json.loads(s); open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/content/02-copy-deck.md'\nL=open(p).read().split('\\n')\nfor i,l in enumerate(L):\n  if l.startswith('| `site.privacy.l.sleep` |'):\n    L.insert(i,\"| `site.privacy.l.voiceFlare` | If you say your Flare instead of taking a photo, up to 10 seconds of your voice goes to our laptop once, over the encrypted link, like a photo. Gemma 4 writes the invite from it. Nothing is kept, and the words it heard never come back. | prose | 45 | | site W4 | ADR-0028 |\"); break\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(L))\np='apps/web/src/routes/(site)/privacy/+page.svelte'\ns=open(p).read(); s=s.replace('''    \"site.privacy.l.voice\",''','''    \"site.privacy.l.voice\",\n    \"site.privacy.l.voiceFlare\",''',1); open(p,'w').write(s)\np='package.json'\ns=open(p).read(); s=s.replace('''    \"e2e:plan\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/plan.ts\",''','''    \"e2e:plan\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/plan.ts\",\n    \"e2e:voice\": \"node apps/web/test/e2e/voice-flare.ts\",''',1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode design/prototype/scripts/copy-lint.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; npx biome check --write . >/dev/null 2>&1; npm run lint 2>&1 | grep -c \"×\"; npm test 2>&1 | grep \"Tests \"","description":"ADR-0028, privacy line, script; lint and tests","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b48b167-826c-4e15-91dd-6583b2246e13","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfvx6P3gHNEE5iCR9BZuq","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"88ca05c0-a427-4bcf-a9eb-1926ee613df8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:49:50.943Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","