{"parentUuid":"6ec23bff-f0f4-46e0-8af2-7146237aa7e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvxrVv9rT7kf4dhuYV8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads as a map now: streets as dotted lines, and the place marked with its facts. Writing ADR-0029, then budget, commit and deploy:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":551965,"output_tokens":1787,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":551965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"59545a8c-9f33-4620-9208-3d63264e92b7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvxrUeFE6GyZ3YrRaPoE","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4831e5e9-6c87-4fd3-880c-dcea531731bc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:59:24.850Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"4831e5e9-6c87-4fd3-880c-dcea531731bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvxrVv9rT7kf4dhuYV8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QrBvM4qFDrGDochVpwJqpq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && cat > docs/architecture/adr/0029-crew-atlas.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-0029: Crew Atlas, your crew's places drawn on the phone\n\nStatus: Accepted (Sun 2026-10-11).\n\n## Context\nThe backlog (#9) asked for a Crew Atlas: the crew's outings, Sparks and Hot spots as a private map of its places, with facts that come only from data. The crew's places live in the sealed Hot spots blob, which only members' phones can open. Each entry has the place key (an OSM id from the map pack), the name, how many times the crew met there and the last day, and no coordinates.\n\n## Decision\n- **Drawing.** The Atlas is drawn on the phone (`lib/components/CrewAtlas.svelte`) at the top of the Crew space, when the crew has places.\n  - **Positions** come from the map pack already on the phone: `place_key` → `items[3]` → lat and lon. Typed places with no OSM id are listed but not drawn.\n  - **Context** comes from the same pack: water, woods, parks, streets and benches inside the box, at most 1,200 points.\n  - **Nothing is fetched for it.** There are no map tiles and no requests, so where the crew meets never leaves the phone. The only network use is the pack file, which the app already loads.\n- **Facts only from data.** \"Met once · Oct 11\" or \"Met 3 times · last Oct 4\", from the blob's count and last day. Dot size grows with the count, at 6 + 3·log2(count) px.\n- **No AI caption.** The backlog imagined Gemma writing the Atlas. Gemma runs on the hub, so a written caption would mean sending the crew's decrypted places off the phone, which breaks the Hot spots promise (BR-K-6). The facts read just as well from templates, so we left the model out.\n- **Accessibility.** The SVG is `role=\"img\"` with a label (\"Map of 3 places your crew met\"), and the list of facts underneath carries the same information as text.\n- **Budget.** The component and the map module load on demand from the Crew page.\n\n## Tests\n`apps/web/test/e2e/sparks.ts` runs on the real stack. It creates a real Hot spot: a Flare lights, a friend arrives, and the host ends it. The Crew page then shows the Atlas with \"West Road · Met once · Oct 11\" (`docs/frontend/evidence/e2e-crew-atlas.png`).\n\n## Consequences\n- The crew gets a map of where it goes outside, private by construction.\n- When a crew uses more than one map pack, the Atlas draws the places found in the pack named by `area`, which is Fairlane by default.\nEOF\nprintf '| [0029](0029-crew-atlas.md) | Crew Atlas drawn on the phone from the sealed Hot spots and the local map pack; no tiles, no request; facts only, no AI caption | Accepted |\\n' >> docs/architecture/adr/README.md\nnpm run budget 2>&1 | grep -E \"/app |/g/|crew|FAIL\"; npx biome check --write apps/web docs >/dev/null 2>&1; npm run lint 2>&1 | grep -c \"×\"; git add apps/web/src/lib/components/CrewAtlas.svelte \"apps/web/src/routes/app/(more)/crew/+page.svelte\" apps/web/test/e2e/sparks.ts design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content docs/architecture/adr docs/frontend/evidence/e2e-crew-atlas.png && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nCrew Atlas: your crew's places on a map drawn on the phone\n\nADR-0029. The sealed Hot spots blob has OSM ids, not coordinates;\nthe map pack already on the phone turns them into positions, and its\nwater, woods, parks, streets and benches give the map its context.\nNo tiles, no request: the crew's places never leave the phone. Facts\nonly from the data (\"Met once · Oct 11\", dot size by count). No AI\ncaption: Gemma runs on the hub and would need the decrypted places.\nLoads on demand on the Crew page. sparks e2e on the real stack: the\nAtlas shows \"West Road · Met once · Oct 11\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"","description":"ADR-0029; budget; commit; push; deploy","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":551965,"output_tokens":1787,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":551965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QrBvM4qFDrGDochVpwJqpq":{"command":"cd \"<project>/flare\" && cat > docs/architecture/adr/0029-crew-atlas.md <<'EOF'\n# ADR-0029: Crew Atlas, your crew's places drawn on the phone\n\nStatus: Accepted (Sun 2026-10-11).\n\n## Context\nThe backlog (#9) asked for a Crew Atlas: the crew's outings, Sparks and Hot spots as a private map of its places, with facts that come only from data. The crew's places live in the sealed Hot spots blob, which only members' phones can open. Each entry has the place key (an OSM id from the map pack), the name, how many times the crew met there and the last day, and no coordinates.\n\n## Decision\n- **Drawing.** The Atlas is drawn on the phone (`lib/components/CrewAtlas.svelte`) at the top of the Crew space, when the crew has places.\n  - **Positions** come from the map pack already on the phone: `place_key` → `items[3]` → lat and lon. Typed places with no OSM id are listed but not drawn.\n  - **Context** comes from the same pack: water, woods, parks, streets and benches inside the box, at most 1,200 points.\n  - **Nothing is fetched for it.** There are no map tiles and no requests, so where the crew meets never leaves the phone. The only network use is the pack file, which the app already loads.\n- **Facts only from data.** \"Met once · Oct 11\" or \"Met 3 times · last Oct 4\", from the blob's count and last day. Dot size grows with the count, at 6 + 3·log2(count) px.\n- **No AI caption.** The backlog imagined Gemma writing the Atlas. Gemma runs on the hub, so a written caption would mean sending the crew's decrypted places off the phone, which breaks the Hot spots promise (BR-K-6). The facts read just as well from templates, so we left the model out.\n- **Accessibility.** The SVG is `role=\"img\"` with a label (\"Map of 3 places your crew met\"), and the list of facts underneath carries the same information as text.\n- **Budget.** The component and the map module load on demand from the Crew page.\n\n## Tests\n`apps/web/test/e2e/sparks.ts` runs on the real stack. It creates a real Hot spot: a Flare lights, a friend arrives, and the host ends it. The Crew page then shows the Atlas with \"West Road · Met once · Oct 11\" (`docs/frontend/evidence/e2e-crew-atlas.png`).\n\n## Consequences\n- The crew gets a map of where it goes outside, private by construction.\n- When a crew uses more than one map pack, the Atlas draws the places found in the pack named by `area`, which is Fairlane by default.\nEOF\nprintf '| [0029](0029-crew-atlas.md) | Crew Atlas drawn on the phone from the sealed Hot spots and the local map pack; no tiles, no request; facts only, no AI caption | Accepted |\\n' >> docs/architecture/adr/README.md\nnpm run budget 2>&1 | grep -E \"/app |/g/|crew|FAIL\"; npx biome check --write apps/web docs >/dev/null 2>&1; npm run lint 2>&1 | grep -c \"×\"; git add apps/web/src/lib/components/CrewAtlas.svelte \"apps/web/src/routes/app/(more)/crew/+page.svelte\" apps/web/test/e2e/sparks.ts design/prototype/src/lib/copy/deck.json docs/content docs/architecture/adr docs/frontend/evidence/e2e-crew-atlas.png && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nCrew Atlas: your crew's places on a map drawn on the phone\n\nADR-0029. The sealed Hot spots blob has OSM ids, not coordinates;\nthe map pack already on the phone turns them into positions, and its\nwater, woods, parks, streets and benches give the map its context.\nNo tiles, no request: the crew's places never leave the phone. Facts\nonly from the data (\"Met once · Oct 11\", dot size by count). No AI\ncaption: Gemma runs on the hub and would need the decrypted places.\nLoads on demand on the Crew page. sparks e2e on the real stack: the\nAtlas shows \"West Road · Met once · Oct 11\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q 2>&1 | tail -1 && npm run deploy:render -- --yes 2>&1 | grep \"deploy started\"","description":"ADR-0029; budget; commit; push; deploy","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"59545a8c-9f33-4620-9208-3d63264e92b7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfvxrUeFE6GyZ3YrRaPoE","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"92d31835-af59-4efb-89b2-e57482b998e8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:59:38.689Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"92d31835-af59-4efb-89b2-e57482b998e8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e567af3c-70c1-46ba-b5a8-ec342a0e3f0d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrBvM4qFDrGDochVpwJqpq","type":"tool_result","content":"ok   /app                          145.7 KB (budget 150)\nok   /app/(more)/crew               99.4 KB\nok   /g/[id]                       144.9 KB (budget 150)\n0\npre-push: secrets, sessions, lint, types, web types and tests ok\nok   deploy started for flare-outside","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc0a4ccd-4de5-4d6f-be37-b6819b73c6b7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:00:39.677Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok   /app                          145.7 KB (budget 150)\nok   /app/(more)/crew               99.4 KB\nok   /g/[id]                       144.9 KB (budget 150)\n0\npre-push: secrets, sessions, lint, types, web types and tests ok\nok   deploy started for flare-outside","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"59545a8c-9f33-4620-9208-3d63264e92b7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":15,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":29},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"92d31835-af59-4efb-89b2-e57482b998e8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slu