{"parentUuid":"cc0a4ccd-4de5-4d6f-be37-b6819b73c6b7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>11545731 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"41b965af-b882-4641-8eba-fdb4e0bea0f2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:00:39.687Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>11545731 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
{"parentUuid":"41b965af-b882-4641-8eba-fdb4e0bea0f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvxxK4x1UGbsoqWKr96R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N6dKc85p8pfb7LAFYhf7Hv","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:<socket>","summary":"Cards, headroom, Voice Flares, Atlas done","message":"Milestone: the website feature cards, JS headroom, Voice Flares and the Crew Atlas are all done and pushed. The last deploy is building now.\n\n**Website feature cards and \"Built with\" (#14)**\n- Ten cards, one per feature that exists today. Each has a 240x360 WebP of the real screen (4 to 10 KB) and one line. A single \"Try a demo\" sits at the end.\n- Unbuilt features get no card, so automations aren't there yet.\n- \"Built with\" lists Gemma 4, Google AI Studio, DigitalOcean (\"paused for now\"), ElevenLabs, Sentry, Mastra, OSM, Render and SvelteKit, each with what it does in Flare. These are plain links; nothing is fetched from those sites.\n- Lighthouse dipped to 99 on mobile home. The hero screenshot had become the LCP, and Chrome's wide lazy margin let 10 card images compete with it. Fixed with a 300 w hero at high priority and card images that load within 400 px of view. All 5 pages are back at 100, mobile and desktop.\n- Side fix: the demo's shrink beat no longer flashes \"0 more to light it\".\n\n**JS headroom**\n- The deck shipped all 900 strings to every page. 197 website-only strings (5.9 KB gzipped) now ship with the website only, via deck.json?site.\n- /app went from 150.3 to 145.7 KB, and /g/ from 149.7 to 144.9 KB.\n- The next big win is zod → zod/mini: zod alone is 22.7 KB gzipped in the app. That touches about 70 schema lines shared with the server, so I've queued it rather than risk it today.\n\n**Voice Flares (ADR-0028)**\n- The open model handles it, on our laptop. Ollama 0.40.2 reports audio for gemma4:e4b, and the model hears WAV passed in the `images` field.\n- On the camera screen, \"Say it instead\" records up to 10 s, converts it on the phone to 16 kHz WAV, and sends it to POST /api/v1/drafts/voice. The server passes it to the hub as a new voice-draft job (asyncapi voiceJob). Voice prompt v1 asks for the same {invite, alt} a photo gets, and enforce() runs on both sides.\n- It is hub-only: there is no cloud tier for voices. The audio is zero-filled, and the words heard never come back.\n- Live, through Render to this Mac's hub: \"Meet at the pond bench\" in 3.6 s.\n- The real-stack e2e (npm run e2e:voice) passes. It plays a macOS `say` fixture into the microphone, then runs a real MediaRecorder recording, the phone's WAV conversion, the server, the hub and Gemma.\n- Hub and contract tests are added, and the privacy page has a new line.\n- The live hub is restarted on the new code.\n\n**Crew Atlas (ADR-0029)**\n- Hot spots have OSM ids, so the phone's own map pack places them on an SVG map, with water, woods, streets and benches for context.\n- No tiles and no requests, so the crew's places never leave the phone.\n- It shows facts only, such as \"Met once · Oct 11\", with dot size by count.\n- There's no Gemma caption on purpose: it would mean sending decrypted places to the hub.\n- The sparks e2e on the real stack shows the Atlas. It loads on demand.\n\n**Tests:** unit tests are 678/62/26. e2e (plan, voice, sparks, demo, loop, telegram, field, pwa) passes, and kit a11y has 0 violations.\n\n**Next:** automations, then Sentry depth, the page audit, fresh-eyes round 4, media and the post.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:<socket>","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Milestone: the website feature cards, JS headroom…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1921,"cache_read_input_tokens":552637,"output_tokens":1373,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_