{"parentUuid":"6801f5db-23ba-4526-8aa4-0daa7338d7f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e567af3c-70c1-46ba-b5a8-ec342a0e3f0d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2b5NGz2QhR1zJYeecCMWD","type":"tool_result","content":"3:Snapshot: Saturday 2026-10-10, entries published up to 16:46 UTC. The deadline is about 38 hours later.\n9:- Launch post: https://dev.to/devteam/join-the-hacktoberfest-open-source-ai-challenge-week-1-touch-grass-2450-in-prizes-across-17-4pom\n11:- Hub with category rules: https://dev.to/challenges/hf26\n19:| Deadline | Sun Oct 11, 11:59 PM PDT = Mon Oct 12, 06:59 UTC = 2:59 AM ET. API `ends_at` is `2026-10-12T06:59:00Z`. |\n20:| Required | A DEV post using the official template, tag `#hf26challenge`. New project built in the window (Oct 5 to Oct 11). One entry per person. Teams up to 4, one post, list teammates' DEV handles. |\n22:| Judging | Writing Quality (weighted most), Relevance, Creativity, Technical Execution, Use of Partner Technology (optional). |\n24:| Prizes | Overall $250 + DEV++ + badge. 6 featured categories at $200. 10 partner categories at $100. 17 winners. One win per person per challenge. |\n25:| Agent session | Optional. \"Judges love it.\" Save with DevRelay, embed with the `agent_session` tag. Uploads are unlisted by default, so make them public and scrub keys. |\n29:### Template sections, in order\n38:8. Prize Categories (list each one, or remove)\n40:Front matter tags in the template: `devchallenge, hf26challenge`.\n42:### Category rules that matter to our stack\n53:Every entry is judged for every category it qualifies for. Partner credits (Render, Tinker, Backboard, ElevenLabs) are claimed at hacktoberfest.com/my/promos.\n60:   - DevRelay `get_articles` for the tag, 10 pages of 100\n64:   The union holds 2,009 `#hf26challenge` posts. Week 1 entries are those published from Oct 5 07:00 UTC on, without the `weekendchallenge` tag or the Weekend template line. **That leaves 813 entries.** All 48 most-reacted Week 1 posts are in the set. The only gap is Oct 5, 18:00 to 20:58 UTC, the first three hours after launch, which has 7 posts in the set.\n65:2. **Text.** Pulled the article text of all 813 from the CDN-served pages, cut at the end of the article body, with HTML comments stripped (the template's comments mention DevRelay and agent sessions). On three spot checks the extracted text was within 1 to 7% of the original markdown's word count.\n67:4. **Reactions.** From DEV API `GET /api/articles?tag=hf26challenge&top=7`.\n144:### Partner categories, by mentions in article text\n146:| Category | Entries | Share | Read |\n179:| [Zero-Screen Dungeon Master](https://dev.to/vidisha_gupta_/zero-screen-dungeon-master-the-voice-only-rpg-where-your-real-walk-drives-the-story-3m68) | Gemma 2 2B on a laptop via Ollama, stories made ahead of time | No, template placeholders left in | GPS beats every 80 m, blind taps through the pocket |\n182:| [TouchGrass](https://dev.to/rajan_mishra_a9f78ad216b4/touchgrass-the-open-ai-agent-that-succeeds-when-you-stop-using-it-3k1e) | Gemma 2 and TabPFN behind FastAPI on Render | Yes, 22 min under an oak | Claims 5 categories with thin evidence; offline claim conflicts with hosting |\n183:| [FieldIssue](https://dev.to/himanshu_748/fieldissue-take-a-walk-report-a-problem-come-back-with-evidence-e40) | Hosted Gemma API, Qwen3-8B fine-tuned on Tinker | Yes, Lucknow, Oct 9 to 10 | Claims 12 categories; publishes a TabPFN result that lost to baseline |\n207:| Category | Entry | What earned it |\n212:| Render | [Tala](https://dev.to/highcenburg/tala-free-audio-to-text-for-my-designer-friend-no-signup-no-credit-card-2o26) | The model itself runs in the Render container (faster-whisper int8). render.yaml Blueprint, Render Postgres, region picked for the friend, auto-deploy, benchmark table. Five other winners hosted on Render and didn't win this category. |\n223:| Tiger Data | [Nivara](https://dev.to/priyanshu_jha_eee132b17e5/my-friend-runs-her-supplements-shop-from-whatsapp-voice-notes-so-i-built-her-a-shop-helper-5785) | Hypertables, continuous aggregates, hybrid search. Claimed 7 categories, won 1. |\n233:5. One specific line per claimed partner category.\n238:What didn't decide it: length (Viva won at about 900 words), reaction counts, numbers in the title (3 of 12), leftover template comments (2 winners had them), or how many categories were claimed (each entry won at most one).\n240:Category bars:\n243:- **Gemma:** being there isn't enough, since 31% of the field names the category. The winner compared model sizes on a test set and let code check the output.\n244:- **MongoDB Atlas:** Atlas has to do something only Atlas does well for the product (GridFS byte-range streaming, hybrid vector plus text search). One more database among seven claimed categories did not win.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dac15839-4179-470d-815a-83e300a87283","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:37:09.326Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3:Snapshot: Saturday 2026-10-10, entries published up to 16:46 UTC. The deadline is about 38 hours later.\n9:- Launch post: https://dev.to/devteam/join-the-hacktoberfest-open-source-ai-challenge-week-1-touch-grass-2450-in-prizes-across-17-4pom\n11:- Hub with category rules: https://dev.to/challenges/hf26\n19:| Deadline | Sun Oct 11, 11:59 PM PDT = Mon Oct 12, 06:59 UTC = 2:59 AM ET. API `ends_at` is `2026-10-12T06:59:00Z`. |\n20:| Required | A DEV post using the official template, tag `#hf26challenge`. New project built in the window (Oct 5 to Oct 11). One entry per person. Teams up to 4, one post, list teammates' DEV handles. |\n22:| Judging | Writing Quality (weighted most), Relevance, Creativity, Technical Execution, Use of Partner Technology (optional). |\n24:| Prizes | Overall $250 + DEV++ + badge. 6 featured categories at $200. 10 partner categories at $100. 17 winners. One win per person per challenge. |\n25:| Agent session | Optional. \"Judges love it.\" Save with DevRelay, embed with the `agent_session` tag. Uploads are unlisted by default, so make them public and scrub keys. |\n29:### Template sections, in order\n38:8. Prize Categories (list each one, or remove)\n40:Front matter tags in the template: `devchallenge, hf26challenge`.\n42:### Category rules that matter to our stack\n53:Every entry is judged for every category it qualifies for. Partner credits (Render, Tinker, Backboard, ElevenLabs) are claimed at hacktoberfest.com/my/promos.\n60:   - DevRelay `get_articles` for the tag, 10 pages of 100\n64:   The union holds 2,009 `#hf26challenge` posts. Week 1 entries are those published from Oct 5 07:00 UTC on, without the `weekendchallenge` tag or the Weekend template line. **That leaves 813 entries.** All 48 most-reacted Week 1 posts are in the set. The only gap is Oct 5, 18:00 to 20:58 UTC, the first three hours after launch, which has 7 posts in the set.\n65:2. **Text.** Pulled the article text of all 813 from the CDN-served pages, cut at the end of the article body, with HTML comments stripped (the template's comments mention DevRelay and agent sessions). On three spot checks the extracted text was within 1 to 7% of the original markdown's word count.\n67:4. **Reactions.** From DEV API `GET /api/articles?tag=hf26challenge&top=7`.\n144:### Partner categories, by mentions in article text\n146:| Category | Entries | Share | Read |\n179:| [Zero-Screen Dungeon Master](https://dev.to/vidisha_gupta_/zero-screen-dungeon-master-the-voice-only-rpg-where-your-real-walk-drives-the-story-3m68) | Gemma 2 2B on a laptop via Ollama, stories made ahead of time | No, template placeholders left in | GPS beats every 80 m, blind taps through the pocket |\n182:| [TouchGrass](https://dev.to/rajan_mishra_a9f78ad216b4/touchgrass-the-open-ai-agent-that-succeeds-when-you-stop-using-it-3k1e) | Gemma 2 and TabPFN behind FastAPI on Render | Yes, 22 min under an oak | Claims 5 categories with thin evidence; offline claim conflicts with hosting |\n183:| [FieldIssue](https://dev.to/himanshu_748/fieldissue-take-a-walk-report-a-problem-come-back-with-evidence-e40) | Hosted Gemma API, Qwen3-8B fine-tuned on Tinker | Yes, Lucknow, Oct 9 to 10 | Claims 12 categories; publishes a TabPFN result that lost to baseline |\n207:| Category | Entry | What earned it |\n212:| Render | [Tala](https://dev.to/highcenburg/tala-free-audio-to-text-for-my-designer-friend-no-signup-no-credit-card-2o26) | The model itself runs in the Render container (faster-whisper int8). render.yaml Blueprint, Render Postgres, region picked for the friend, auto-deploy, benchmark table. Five other winners hosted on Render and didn't win this category. |\n223:| Tiger Data | [Nivara](https://dev.to/priyanshu_jha_eee132b17e5/my-friend-runs-her-supplements-shop-from-whatsapp-voice-notes-so-i-built-her-a-shop-helper-5785) | Hypertables, continuous aggregates, hybrid search. Claimed 7 categories, won 1. |\n233:5. One specific line per claimed partner category.\n238:What didn't decide it: length (Viva won at about 900 words), reaction counts, numbers in the title (3 of 12), leftover template comments (2 winners had them), or how many categories were claimed (each entry won at most one).\n240:Category bars:\n243:- **Gemma:** being there isn't enough, since 31% of the field names the category. The winner compared model sizes on a test set and let code check the output.\n244:- **MongoDB Atlas:** Atlas has to do something only Atlas does well for the product (GridFS byte-range streaming, hybrid vector plus text search). One more database among seven claimed categories did not win.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7d900420-274a-4f11-acb4-d33b692eac98","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":27},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":