{"parentUuid":"1e6e6011-0cc0-42f1-a5c5-22d83a5b954c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e567af3c-70c1-46ba-b5a8-ec342a0e3f0d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9qajuEyZYUFPNQ2Jgyrtb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file <project>/flare/docs/post/media/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"25bd2719-81fc-44cc-8a37-6a8eaa853df4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:40:34.528Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"<project>/flare/docs/post/media/README.md","content":"# Post media\n\nThese are real screenshots from the real app on the real stack: the server, the hub running Gemma 4 E4B on this Mac, the engine and PGlite. They were taken in Chrome at iPhone size (390x844 @2x), JPEG quality 78, on Sun 2026-10-11 at about 15:45 ET, by `scripts/capture-media.ts`. Re-run it with `npm run build && node scripts/capture-media.ts`.\n\nThe host picks a real photo through the app's own \"Pick a photo\": Eagle Lake, Acadia National Park, public domain (NPS, see [docs/credits/photos.md](../../credits/photos.md)). The fake camera's test pattern isn't used. The Ember shot jumps 31 minutes with the e2e test clock, which only exists with an in-memory database. Nothing else is staged.\n\n| File | Moment | From |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 00-home.jpg | Home: golden hour, the weather, the nearest green spot, Light a Flare | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-words.jpg | The photo developed, with the invite Gemma 4 wrote from it (\"Meet by the quiet water's edge\") | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-send.jpg | Send it: how many it needs, where you'll be | capture-media.ts |\n| 01-host-sent.jpg | Sent | capture-media.ts |\n| 02-friend-invite.jpg | The friend's invite: photo, words, walk time, the count, I'm in | capture-media.ts |\n| 03-friend-lit.jpg, 03-host-lit.jpg | It's lit, on both phones, with Tell the chat on the host's | capture-media.ts |\n| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: 400 m. A headless browser has no compass, so it asks to hold the phone flat | capture-media.ts |\n| 04b-demo-compass-ahead.jpg | Find them with a heading: \"The bench by the willow is straight ahead\" | e2e demo |\n| 05-friend-spark.jpg | Leaving a Spark, with Say it (Voice Spark) | capture-media.ts |\n| 06-friend-ember.jpg | Needs 3, one yes, 31 minutes later: the smaller plan at West Road | capture-media.ts |\n| 07-telegram-card-kindling.png, 07-telegram-card-lit.png | The Telegram card, Kindling and Lit, from the server's own renderer | earlier capture; the renderer is unchanged |\n| 08-voice-flare-send.png | A Voice Flare: \"Meet at the pond bench\", written by Gemma 4 from what was said, with no photo | e2e voice-flare (real hub) |\n| 09-crew-atlas.png | The Crew Atlas, drawn on the phone from the sealed Hot spots | e2e sparks (real stack) |\n| 10-plan-lit.png | A Plan solved at the deadline: step 3, the biggest step all three can do | e2e plan (real stack) |\n| 11-demo-friend-view.jpg | The demo's friend view | e2e demo |\n| 12-site-home-phone.png, 13-site-feature-cards.png | The website on a phone, and the feature cards on desktop | local build |\n| sim/fairlane-sim-42.gif | \"A Saturday in Fairlane, played by 48 friends\": the simulation (labelled Simulation) | tools/sim |\n\nStill to add: the founder's iPhone screen recording from [shot-list.md](../shot-list.md), and a Sentry trace screenshot from the live project (it needs the founder's Sentry login).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":17,"newStart":1,"newLines":27,"lines":[" # Post media"," ","-Real screenshots from the real app on the real stack (server, hub with Gemma 4 E4B, engine, PGlite), Chrome at iPhone size (390x844 @2x), JPEG quality 78. Captured Sun 2026-10-11 ~07:45 ET. The Ember shot used the e2e test clock to jump 30 minutes; nothing else is staged. Telegram cards come from the server's own renderer (`apps/server/src/telegram/card.ts`).","+These are real screenshots from the real app on the real stack: the server, the hub running Gemma 4 E4B on this Mac, the engine and PGlite. They were taken in Chrome at iPhone size (390x844 @2x), JPEG quality 78, on Sun 2026-10-11 at about 15:45 ET, by `scripts/capture-media.ts`. Re-run it with `npm run build && node scripts/capture-media.ts`."," ","-| File | Moment |","-| --- | --- |","-| 01-host-words.jpg | The photo developed, six words from the model |","-| 01-host-send.jpg | Send it: how many it needs, what's near |","-| 01-host-sent.jpg | Sent |","-| 02-friend-invite.jpg | The friend's invite |","-| 03-friend-lit.jpg, 03-host-lit.jpg | It's lit, on both phones |","-| 04-friend-compass.jpg | Find them: distance and spoken direction |","-| 05-friend-spark.jpg | Leaving a Spark |","-| 06-friend-ember.jpg, 06-host-ember.jpg | 30 minutes without enough yeses: the smaller plan |","-| 07-telegram-card-kindling.png, 07-telegram-card-lit.png | The Telegram card, Kindling and Lit |","+The host picks a real photo through the app's own \"Pick a photo\": Eagle Lake, Acadia National Park, public domain (NPS, see [docs/credits/photos.md](../../credits/photos.md)). The fake camera's test pattern isn't used. The Ember shot jumps 31 minutes with the e2e test clock, which only exists with an in-memory database. Nothing else is staged."," ","-Still to add: [FIELD] photos from the field test, and the iPhone screen recording from [shot-list.md](../shot-list.md).","+| File | Moment | From |","+| --- | --- | --- |","+| 00-home.jpg | Home: golden hour, the weather, the nearest green spot, Light a Flare | capture-media.ts |","+| 01-host-words.jpg | The photo developed, with the invite Gemma 4 wrote from it (\"Meet by the quiet water's edge\") | capture-media.ts |","+| 01-host-send.jpg | Send it: how many it needs, where you'll be | capture-media.ts |","+| 01-host-sent.jpg | Sent | capture-media.ts |","+| 02-friend-invite.jpg | The friend's invite: photo, words, walk time, the count, I'm in | capture-media.ts |","+| 03-frie