\n37:| hard_20 | 18/20 | 20/20 | 10/20 | 18/20 | 19/20 |\n39:| fresh_hard_40 | 15/40 | 40/40 (dev set) | 20/40 | 38/40 | 38/40 |\n40:| blind_40 | 20/40 | 30/40 | 25/40 | not run | 38/40 |\n56:The LoRA is eval-only, served by Tinker sampling; no GGUF or Ollama export (no Qwen3.5-4B on the hub, and\n67:python eval.py rules && python eval.py base && python eval.py lora && python report.py\n79:4. If a model is wanted on the hub later: pull the base, download the adapter, convert to GGUF, add it to\n80:   Ollama. Needs a yes for the downloads.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3dc05907-2c74-4917-916f-093b3915f045","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:40:55.522Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"7:- The answer is unchanged: `{steps: 4 x {step, label, minutes}, tier, ms}`, always through `enforceLadder()`, the template on any failure.\n27:| evals/harness/tasks/ladder-agent.ts, evals/datasets/ladder-asks.json (L13, `keep`) | `npm run eval -- ladder-agent` |\n44:  - neither eval run had a first answer fail the guard (0 of 13, and 0 of 18 in a probe with 5 harder asks), so the retry never ran;\n48:## Eval numbers (local Ollama, gemma4:e4b-it-q4_K_M, 13 asks, 2026-10-11 12:00 ET, hub retry none)\n56:| p95, all 13 | ≤ 8000 ms | 5527 ms | 5127 ms |\n57:| p95, 12 original asks | ≤ 6500 ms (agent) | 5172 ms | 5127 ms |\n59:| Tool weather matches the plan's window | all | n/a | 7/7 |\n61:- **Medians:** 4432 ms current, 4312 ms agent.\n62:- **Agent overhead:** median 12 ms, p95 293 ms.\n65:- **Same run with `EVAL_LADDER_RETRY=corrective`:** same bars; p95 5332 ms current, 5638 ms agent (`evals/reports/ladder-agent-hub-retry-corrective.md`).\n66:- **Before the guard fix (11:15):** p95 on all 13 was 8028 ms current and 8026 ms agent, and L13 fell to the template on both.\n----\n1:# Handoff 11: Tinker LoRA for the conditions parser, then rules taught by it\n10:1. A Qwen3.5-4B LoRA trained on Tinker read far more new phrasings than the rules parser (fresh_hard_40:\n11:   38/40 vs 15/40). It runs on Tinker's