{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:45:52.396Z","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:<socket>\" from-session=\"local_beb3cc8c-e162-46cc-bd0a-f870e8717ebd\" hop-chain=\"e1bd9b33a07bd8c38e68ae6a,d6d9bf2e945799a80139a5bf,e1bd9b33a07bd8c38e68ae6a,d6d9bf2e945799a80139a5bf,e1bd9b33a07bd8c38e68ae6a,d6d9bf2e945799a80139a5bf\" from-name=\"Flare Manager(founders CTO)\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nI checked the post draft: clean writing, 0 banned words, 0 em dashes, all claims tied to proof. Before the founder's review:\n\n1. **Template line:** check it against the official submission template. The link should be the Week 1 page, https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week1-2026-10-05, not /challenges/hf26, unless the template says otherwise. Check the required tags too.\n2. **Tighten to about 2,300 to 2,500 words.** Writing counts most, and every winner's post was sharp. Cut repeated explanations; the numbers can live in tables.\n3. **Open with a scene, not a definition.** For example, the group chat where \"we should go for a walk\" dies, then the moment a friend with low vision hears Gemma describe the photo and the compass walks them in. Keep the founder [FIELD] quote, but write a suggested version they can accept or edit.\n4. **A 5-row \"At a glance\" table near the top:** what happens / the open piece doing it / proof link.\n5. **Prize Categories:** one line per category, linking to its signature-moment section.\n6. **My Agent Session:** keep a clear placeholder for the DevRelay embed.\n\nThen fix fresh-eyes round 4 when it reports, and recapture any screenshot that changes.\n</cross-session-message>"}
