{"parentUuid":"022fdd4f-f00c-40fd-acc2-2002d7a2fa45","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fd88ddca-c246-47fd-aaf8-44796a9bb0a3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WruDZgrHYEXXgU9tfA8V7g","type":"tool_result","content":"The visible portion contains four prize categories. Mastra, Entire, ElevenLabs, and Sentry do not appear in it, and the excerpt ends partway through the Backboard listing, so they may be in the unseen part of the page.\n\n**Visible categories**\n\n1. **Best Use of Arduino** ($200 USD + exclusive winner badge): Build with an Arduino UNO Q, such as running a model on the board, building a physical agent that senses and acts, or optimizing a model for it with Qualcomm AI Hub.\n2. **Best Use of DigitalOcean** ($200 USD + exclusive winner badge): Build or deploy on DigitalOcean, such as hosting an app or agent, running an open-weight model on a GPU Droplet, or building on the Gradient AI Platform.\n3. **Best Use of Gemma** ($200 USD + exclusive winner badge): Use Gemma, Google's open-weight model, by running it locally, fine-tuning it, or serving it through Google Cloud or another provider.\n4. **Best Use of Backboard** ($100 USD, prize text cut off): Build with R-CLI, compare open-weight models through one Backboard API key, or add memory and RAG to an open-source project's assistant.\n\n**Partner categories**\n\nThe page lists \"$100 for each winner\" under a \"Partner categories\" heading. Backboard appears under that heading, so it is a partner category. The page doesn't clearly label the first three as featured, so I haven't assumed they are.\n\n**Your specific checks**\n\n- **DigitalOcean:** Yes, listed above.\n- **Gemma:** Yes, listed above.\n- **Mastra, Entire, ElevenLabs, Sentry:** Not in the visible content. Check the rest of the page.\n\n[WebFetch note: this page's text is 275858 characters long and the answer above covers only characters 100000 to 200000; the final 75858 were not read — to read on, call WebFetc