{"parentUuid":"3f3b0d09-eef2-4c77-bdcc-ae4348993c0b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fd88ddca-c246-47fd-aaf8-44796a9bb0a3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YcMifPnVipGHYP7vA9TGZY","type":"tool_result","content":"**Yes, these exist:**\n\n- **Best Use of Mastra** ($100 partner category): Orchestrate an agent over open models, add memory and tools to a chat agent, or build a workflow that triages GitHub issues.\n- **Best Use of Entire** ($100): Share the agent sessions behind your project in the write-up, or search past agent work to explain why code exists.\n- **Best Use of ElevenLabs** ($100): Give an open-source agent a voice, transcribe audio for a local model, or generate narration for your demo.\n- **Best Use of Sentry Agent Tracing** ($100): Show how your agent is set up and how it performs (latency, tokens, cost), then explain what you found and how you debugged it, with traces or screenshots.\n- **Best Use of Tinker** is listed as a featured ($200) category, but its requirement isn't in the text provided.\n\n**Other remaining categories in this section:**\n\n- **Best Use of GitHub Copilot** ($100): Build with Copilot's coding agent, the Copilot CLI, or the new Copilot app, automate with GitHub Actions, or review contributors' PRs with Copilot.\n- **Best Use of MongoDB Atlas** ($100): Use Atlas as your data layer, such as for vector search, agent long-term memory, or a database behind an open-weight model app.\n- **Best Use of SerpApi** ($100): Give an agent live web search, ground a RAG app in fresh results, or track news for an open-source project.\n- **Best Use of Temporal** ($100): Wrap your agent in a Temporal workflow so it survives failures, retries flaky tool calls, and resumes where it left off.\n- **Best Use of Tiger Data** ($100): Store embeddings with pgvector, run hybrid keyword and vector search, or let an agent manage a database through Tiger MCP.\n\nThe text also lists Render, TabPFN, Arduino, DigitalOcean, Gemma, and Backboard as featured or partner categories, but their requirements are outside the provided section.\n\n**Agent session embed rule:** No specific embed tag is required. The page says, \"Save your agent session with DevRelay and embed it in your post, or link to it. It's optional, but it helps the judges understand your process.\" The only required tags are #devchallenge and #hf26challenge."}]},"uuid":"f4f990e8-3e1a-440d-ace7-f9ac06f8d976","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:46:34.883Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":370365,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Yes, these exist:**\n\n- **Best Use of Mastra** ($100 partner category): Orchestrate an agent over open models, add memory and tools to a chat agent, or build a workflow that triages GitHub issues.\n- **Best Use of Entire** ($100): Share the agent sessions behind your project in the write-up, or search past agent work to explain why code exists.\n- **Best Use of ElevenLabs** ($100): Give an open-source agent a voice, transcribe audio for a local model, or generate narration for your demo.\n- **Best Use of Sentry Agent Tracing** ($100): Show how your agent is set up and how it performs (latency, tokens, cost), then explain what you found and how you debugged it, with traces or screenshots.\n- **Best Use of Tinker** is listed as a featured ($200) category, but its requirement isn't in the text provided.\n\n**Other remaining categories in this section:**\n\n- **Best Use of GitHub Copilot** ($100): Build with Copilot's coding agent, the Copilot CLI, or the new Copilot app, automate with GitHub Actions, or review contributors' PRs with Copilot.\n- **Best Use of MongoDB Atlas** ($100): Use Atlas as your data layer, such as for vector search, agent long-term memory, or a database behind an open-weight model app.\n- **Best Use of SerpApi** ($100): Give an agent live web search, ground a RAG app in fresh results, or track news for an open-source project.\n- **Best Use of Temporal** ($100): Wrap your agent in a Temporal workflow so it survives failures, retries flaky tool calls, and resumes where it left off.\n- **Best Use of Tiger Data** ($100): Store embeddings with pgvector, run hybrid keyword and vector search, or let an agent manage a database through Tiger MCP.\n\nThe text also lists Render, TabPFN, Arduino, DigitalOcean, Gemma, and Backboard as featured or partner categories, but their requirements are outside the provided section.\n\n**Agent session embed rule:** No specific embed tag is required. The page says, \"Save your agent session with DevRelay and embed it in your post, or link to it. It's optional, but it helps the judges understand your process.\" The only required tags are #devchallenge and #hf26challenge.","durationMs":10954,"url":"https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week1-2026-10-05"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"59727187-f19b-4934-96f9-481fad020481","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"<project>/flare","root":"<project>/flare","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":27},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/flare","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"<project>/flare","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f3b0d09-eef2-4c77-bdcc-ae4348993c0b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"<project>/flare","sessionId":"904c52d9-f200-4552-8ce5-05e400952efa","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"wondrous-tumbling-meteor"}
